+## N1: duet benchmarking (S/M)
+
+Status: done. **Not adopted**: the null arm's intervals leave [0.97, 1.03] in both runs (five of six intervals). Wall clock stays at b = 0.41; N3 and N21 are skipped.
+
+**Design.** `lab/duet.sh <A> <B|null> <layouts> <rounds> <Bench=N>...`: each arm built at the given number of code layouts with `verify/lrab.sh`'s pads (copied to `lab/pads.sh`). Per round, layout and benchmark, both test binaries start at once (both spin on a file, then `exec`), pinned with `taskset` to vCPUs 1 and 2 (different guest cores; swapped on even rounds), `GOMAXPROCS=1`, the same `-test.benchtime=Nx`; ratio B/A of their ns/op. Then A alone on the same vCPU (solo ns/op, for the mutual-slowdown report). Summary per benchmark: geomean of B/A over rounds × layouts and a 95% t-interval of the log ratios (df = pairs − 1). The null arm is `B = null`: A's binaries run against themselves.
+
+N per benchmark (measured part ≈ 0.4–0.5 s at the lab's ns/op): CheckAndTouchHit 3,000,000; TouchAndCount 2,500,000; InsertSteady 1,000,000.
+
+Commands: run 1 `lab/duet.sh HEAD null 4 6 CheckAndTouchHit=3000000 TouchAndCount=2500000 InsertSteady=1000000`; run 2, started after run 1 ends, the same with `SEED0=4` (layouts 5–8).
