+**Rule** (as the prompt states it). Duet becomes this lab's wall-clock method if in both runs the null arm's interval on CheckAndTouchHit, TouchAndCount and InsertSteady lies within [0.97, 1.03] (six intervals). Then b_duet = max(0.02, 2 × the largest |1 − null geomean| of the six), and "faster" = geomean below 1 − b_duet with its interval below 1.00 ("slower" symmetrically). Otherwise wall clock stays at b = 0.41 and the cachegrind/flood/deterministic readings; N3 and N21 are then skipped. Also reported: duet/solo ns/op (how much two copies slow each other).
