+- The smallest passing split is **50 register bits + 40 identity bits** (H/48; 1 1 2 4 8 16 16 16; 8 buckets, counters 4 4 5 6 7 8 8 8). It is D19's "H/48, 8 buckets" (D19: 0.064, mean only): this reading adds its windows: the 1 s error falls 30% (0.2138 → 0.1495), 5 s 10%, and 15–60 s stay within 1% of HEAD.
