+Rule (2) needs p95 ≤ 0.03 at 1% for each W ≥ 5 s, pooled over the three loads: at W = 5 s and 15 s every load is above 0.03, so the pooled p95 is too (more than 5% of each load's queries exceed 0.03); W = 30 s is above at two loads of three; only W = 60 s holds. The error is what a 1% sample of slots gives (≈ 2,350 slots on tfbench's table; a few hundred active keys at W = 5 s): relative sd ≈ 1/√(active keys sampled). It falls as 1/√(sample): 10% reaches ≤ 4.1% at 5 s and ≤ 2.1% at 15 s.
