+## N7: work counters as a deterministic tail measure; incremental sweep re-read (M)
+
+Status: done. **E11b: candidate** (every criterion holds in work units). The counters are a tool (report only).
+
+**Why.** Wall-clock tails can't be read here (lab E11b's max bottomed at the VM's 2–3 ms stalls). A single-goroutine call's work, counted in the code, is deterministic.
+
+**Counters** (patch `go/verify/experiments/next-n7-work.patch`): build tag `tfwork`. Without it `workAdd(kind, n)` is an empty function the compiler removes (the gates are read without the tag); with it, plain package counters (single-goroutine use only, documented). Kinds and where they count:
+- `lines`: table lines read: `find`, `slotWords`, each line of `claimAt`'s scans (free-slot pass, every deepening pass, the eviction scoring pass), the alternate line `relocate` computes, each line `warmLine` loads;
+- `stash`: stash and wait-room sets read (`stashTable.set`);
+- `ghost`: overflow-table buckets read or written (`ghost.slot`'s bucket count per call);
+- `hot`: hot entries read or written (the hot-entry functions of hot.go that touch an entry);
+- `sweep`: words the overflow table's `advance` visits;
+- `decay`: lines decay's sweep visits (`sweepLine`).
+- **work** (one number per call) = lines + stash + ghost + hot + ⌈sweep / 8⌉ + decay, roughly cache lines (8 words per line). Each kind is also reported on its own.
+
+**Workloads** (`TF_EXP=1 go test -tags tfwork -run '^TestWork' -v .`, in the patch; per call: p50, p99, p99.9, max of work, and the max and mean of each kind):
+1. tfbench's churn stream at loads 1.00 / 1.10 / 1.15 (CheckAndTouchAt);
+2. heavy16x at quarter scale (`$LAB/h2h/heavy16x.trace`, `TF_TRACE`), replayed as `h2h run` does (TouchAt of HashUint64(key), the trace's window);
+3. lab E11's sweep workload (Capacity 2^18, 2M keys × 4 TouchAt over 7 overflow-table slices; calls after the first slice, as E11b);
+4. unseen inserts at 85% load (InsertSteady's pattern on Capacity 200,000: unseen keys at Capacity per horizon, 400,000 warm-up calls, then 200,000 measured), Background off and on; with Background on the placer runs by hand after each call (`bgManual`, as `TestPlacerInterference`), and its work is reported separately per call (it is off the call path).
+Targets 9 and 11 context only: report, no rule.
+
+**E11b re-read in work units.** Arms: main + counters, and main + `lab-e11b-incremental-sweep.patch` (from origin/lab/experiments-2026-11, applies to 2ca617b) + counters (its `sweepWord` counts the words it visits, the same kind as `advance`); workload 3. **Rule** (E11b's criteria in work units, declared before reading): candidate if (1) the max work per call is at least 10x lower than main's; (2) p99.9 work is not higher; (3) gates identical on main + E11b (no tag); (4) `go test -race -count=20 -run '^TestGhost' .` passes on main + E11b. Single runs: the counts are deterministic (checked by running main's arm twice).
