+## N8: backyard placement, simulated (M)
+
+Status: done. **Not worth writing**: every arm fails three or more of the rule's five criteria.
+
+**Question.** Targets 9 and 11 come from moves: at 85% load 44% of first touches find both lines full (S38), and N7 read the cuckoo search as the insert tail (p99 32 lines at 85%, 757 at 97.8%). Iceberg hashing (front yard + small backyard, never move) and Morton filters' overflow bits (most absent lookups read one bucket) suggest a placement with no moves. Caveat (Iceberg, Remark 2): its guarantees need large front buckets; Clepsydra's lines hold 4.
+
+**Model** (test-only, like D10's placement oracle; `TF_EXP=1 go test -tags tfwork -run '^TestBackyard$' -v .`, patch `go/verify/experiments/next-n8-backyard.patch`, applied after `next-n7-work.patch`, whose counters read HEAD on the same stream):
+- Stream: tfbench's churn (internal/workload; Capacity 200,000; loads 1.00 / 1.10 / 1.15 = 85 / 94 / 97.8% slot load; seeds 2 / 3 / 4; horizon 60,000 ticks), each op a CheckAndTouch of key h.
+- Front yard: HEAD's two candidate lines (HEAD's `primary` and `alt`, 4 slots each). A slot is free if empty or its entry's last touch is older than the horizon. No entry ever moves.
+- Backyard: buckets of 8 slots (2 cache lines each), two candidates per key by other hash bits (mix64 of h), sized as a fraction b of the front's slots, b ∈ {5%, 10%, 15%}, in two families: **added** (front = HEAD's lines, backyard on top) and **carved** (total slots = HEAD's; front lines = HEAD's / (1 + b)).
+- Per-line overflow bit: line p's bit is set while any live backyard entry has p as its primary line (exact, as if cleared the moment the last such entry expires: the optimistic case for lookups).
+- Touch of key h: read p (1 line); match a home entry there, else read a (1 line) and match a displaced entry, else if bit(p) read both backyard buckets (4 lines). Found and live: touched. Otherwise an **unseen insert**: the placement pass reads p and a again (2 lines, HEAD's claimAt does the same), takes a free slot in p, then a; else the less loaded backyard bucket (its 4 lines already read if bit(p) was set, else +4); if both buckets are full of live entries, a **forced eviction** (the least recently touched of the 16 goes; a live key lost).
+- Line reads are counted as N7 counts HEAD's (each read of a line by a pass counts, re-reads included), so the two are comparable.
+- Absent lookups: at the end of each stream, 1,000,000 never-inserted keys: line reads, and identity comparisons (entries a key would be compared with: home entries of p, displaced entries of a, and when bit(p) every live entry of both buckets). FPR model = comparisons × 2^−28 (28-bit identity as today; D11's 3.40 at 85% gives HEAD 1.27e-8).
+- HEAD, same stream: the filter with N7's counters; a call is an unseen insert if ground truth has no touch of h within the horizon; absent lookups are `ContainsAt` of the same 1,000,000 keys.
+- Memory: (front + backyard slots) × 16 B + one bit per front line, per key of Capacity (HEAD's table: 18.8 B/key).
+
+**Output.** Per arm and load: unseen-insert line reads (mean, p99), absent-lookup line reads (mean) and comparisons, FPR model, backyard fill (peak live / slots), forced evictions, B/key; HEAD beside it (lines per unseen insert, absent lookup, evictions).
+
+**Rule** (the prompt's). An implementation is worth writing only if some arm, at 85% load, has unseen-insert line reads ≥ 50% lower than HEAD's in both mean and p99, absent-lookup line reads ≤ 1.05 × HEAD's, FPR model ≤ 2.5e-8, total memory ≤ 20 B/key; and at 94% load no forced eviction.
+
+**Readings.** `git apply --directory=go` N7's then N8's patch; `TF_EXP=1 go test -tags tfwork -count=1 -run '^TestBackyard$' -v .` (11 s; `lab/readings/n8.txt`). Line reads per unseen insert (mean / p99), absent-lookup line reads, identity comparisons per absent lookup, FPR model, forced evictions (live keys lost), keys sent to the backyard, memory:
