+By the rule (85% load unless stated): (1) insert line reads ≥ 50% lower in mean **and** p99: p99 falls 67% in every arm (24 → 8), but the mean falls at most 40% (8.107 → 4.829): **fails** in every arm. Under this accounting (N7's: the placement pass re-reads both lines, as claimAt does) a no-move insert can't cost less than 4 line reads, so 50% (4.05) was within 0.05 of the floor. (2) absent-lookup lines ≤ 1.05 × 2.000: 2.675–3.668 (+34% to +83%): **fails** everywhere: 11–15% of first touches go to the backyard, so 17–42% of lines carry the overflow bit. (3) FPR ≤ 2.5e-8: holds only for the 5% arms (2.49e-8). (4) ≤ 20 B/key: holds except added 10% and 15%. (5) no forced eviction at 94%: **fails** in every arm (48,247–121,269 live keys lost; even at 85% every arm but added 15% loses tens of thousands).
