+**Verdict: candidate**, with two things for your decision: (a) it is the lock-based design, not the prompt's single-CAS one: conditional touches of keys sharing one of 64 stripes serialize, and each call does a read and a touch; (b) as a limiter it is safe but conservative: Upper counts a cut bucket whole, so with the 2.5 s unit a 1 s window admits about 65% of its limit on one hot key and 30% across 1,000 keys (5 s: 53% and 30%), and on the velocity workload it agrees with an exact limiter on 67–71% of requests. The guarantee holds through any Upper; a tighter limiter needs a tighter Upper on short windows (target 7's gap again, N4b's geometry or D19's side information).
