+## N20b: an additive correction to the uniform cut fraction (follow-up arm)
+
+Status: done. **Not adopted.**
+
+**Design.** N20's data, contexts and code, except what a cell holds: δ = Σ (inside − uniform fraction × spread events) / Σ spread events over its training queries, and the estimate uses the uniform fraction + δ (clipped to [0, 1]); cells with < 50 queries use δ = 0. So within a bin the interpolation stays, and the table only moves it by what the training traffic says the uniform model misses in that context.
+
+**Rule:** N20's, unchanged (mean −0.003 on both held-out sets; no window more than 5% worse on either). Written after N20's numbers; the rule is not relaxed, the arm is new.
+
+**Readings** (`TF_EXP=1 N20_ADDITIVE=1 N20_MAWI=<file> go test -run '^TestFittedCut$' -v .`; patch `go/verify/experiments/next-n20-fitted-cut.patch`, which holds both arms and N4's `velWorkloadSeed`; `lab/readings/n20.txt`):
