+| MAWI first half (training) | 0.3177 → 0.3070 | 0.0446 → 0.0435 | 0.0286 → 0.0302 | 0.0130 → 0.0172 | 0.0163 → 0.0163 | 0.0841 → 0.0828 |
+
+By the rule: the mean rises on both held-out sets (needs −0.003), and MAWI's 5 s (+13%), 30 s (+5.3%) and 60 s (+35%) are more than 5% worse: **fails**. **Verdict: not adopted.** The correction learns something of the training traffic (−0.0012 there, −3.4% at 1 s) that doesn't carry to the trace's other half or to the synthetic shapes: the cut bucket's position-and-pattern context holds little that generalizes beyond what the uniform spread already gives. With N8–N12 and N4b, the register's short-window error is a question of information (more bits, recent exact ticks), not of a better reading of the same bits.
